00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:49.460
In fact, from my perspective the most interesting part of this new DCEU Joker

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.740
has come from the fans, nay, the theorists.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:58.080
You see, back before Suicide Squad hit theaters, HECK, even before Batman V Superman hit theaters

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:03.280
Online theorists were guessing that the Joker wasn't quite who he said he was

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.740
That he wasn't just some off-the-street criminal mastermind like he's been in

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:08.540
every other cinematic incarnation

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:13.540
But that he was instead Batman's favorite Boy Wonder, Robin.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:17.480
Robin, who had somehow been transformed into a psychotic madman

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:20.140
and for those of you who think you've already heard this theory, well..

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:23.060
Stick around because I think you're going to be surprised by this one.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:28.420
Now, as far as I can tell this fan series started gathering evidence with a Reddit post from Jason-G169

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:33.120
back in 2015 who started analyzing all the promotional materials around holes in these movies

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:39.360
and legitimately there ARE a LOT of weird coincidences here: The bird tattoo on the Joker's arm,

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:43.680
the way Joker holds his cane in the Suicide Squad poster being similar to how Robin's suit

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.520
is positioned holding his lance in Batman V Superman,

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.220
the bullet holes in the Robin suit hanging in the Batcave

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:53.860
matching strange dots on Jared Leto's shoulders and promo shots for Suicide Squad

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:55.720
And the fact that in the video game Arkham Knight,

00:02:55.720 --> 00:03:00.280
one of Batman's former Robins has a scar of a J on his face left there by the Joker,

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:06.000
a scar that just so happens to be in the same placement as the tattoo the Joker has in Suicide Squad.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.600
Legitimately when you look at all that evidence laid out there's a fair amount of to go off of

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:16.480
But then the buzz kill train named David Ayer, director of Suicide Squad *WHOO WHOOOO!!*

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:19.920
rolled into the station and killed the theory DEAD.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.300
When asked what the most outlandish thing he'd heard about the movie was, he responded with this:

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:28.880
"That the Joker is Jason Todd." (Interviewer) "Really!?" "That ain't the case."

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:33.960
Now, if you're NOT a Batman super fan, let me catch you up: Jason Todd in the comics is one of the

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:38.600
three main characters to have taken on the mantle of Robin over the years and I say "ONE OF"

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:43.040
because just like there've been multiple Jokers so too have there been multiple Robins.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:46.000
You have the original Dick Grayson who eventually moves on from being

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:50.280
Batman's sidekick and turns into the hero Nightwing. Jason Todd is the next Robin.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:54.300
At least until the Joker kidnaps him, beats him with a crowbar and blows him up in a warehouse.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.600
*O-O-O-OVERKILL!!*

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:59.660
And then there's Tim Drake who tries to alleviate Batman's depression about

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:02.180
Jason Todd's murder by becoming the new Robin.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:07.080
it's also worth noting that all three of them have, at one point or another in the comics

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.680
turned into the joker

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:15.420
So the idea of one of these characters turning into a tatted out jugalo isn't as absurd as it might seem

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:18.220
turning into mister J is like a write of passage for the  boy wonder,

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:21.000
right next to stop crime in a green speedo

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.680
in the comic, dark knight strikes again, Dick Grason

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:27.800
is fired for bieng robin and becomes the joker, Jason Todd after getting

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.500
killed in a death in the family by the joker, gets

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:31.800
gets resurrected via Lazarus pit

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.540
because, Hey! if you've got a pit that'll revive your dead

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.800
well, you use dat thing

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:38.700
upon his return, he takes on the role of the villian

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:39.480
RED HOOD

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:43.580
Which just so happens to be the Joker's original criminal identity

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:48.360
And then theres tim drake, who in the 2000 movie Batman Beyond Return Of The Joker,

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:54.140
Got himself kidnapped and brainwashed by the OG Joker, who then implants a micro chip into his neck

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:58.380
that mutates his DNA to make him into a Joker clone.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:02.940
He is litteraly a werewolf , exept for hair, he has white clown makeup, and a killer laugh.

